  "confirmed_observations": [
    "Both arms initially encounter a covered search input. Reference uses Enter to submit; candidate inspects the covering CAPTCHA dialog. They select different products and use different subsequent retrieval strategies.",
    "Reference events 58/59 probe several feedback URLs. The HTML feedback endpoint says System is busy; the pc/searchEvaluation.do endpoint returns JSON. Events 62/63 retain that JSON.",
    "Candidate events 58/59 encounter the same busy-page class on an HTML feedback endpoint for a different product. Events 114/115 and 118/119 receive empty records from a legacy feedback service for several product IDs.",
    "No candidate JavaScript tool-call source contains searchEvaluation. This proves the reference's successful endpoint was not explicitly called in recorded candidate code; it does not prove what internal page scripts requested.",
    "Candidate additionally inspects scripts, guesses review API names and tries alternative product/page forms. After 71 steps and 521.658 seconds it reports a qualifying product and an unresolved review-text blocker. Reference delivers a review summary after 27 steps and 132.961 seconds.",
    "Reference event 87 contains nine sort-parameter trials. Every trial returns the same 20-date sequence and none is descending. The claimed latest sort parameter was not validated as effective.",
    "Reference event 90 fetches six pages (120 reviews), locally sorts by date and selects 60. That establishes recency within the retrieved subset, not globally most-recent coverage of all 2,140 reviews."
